one is selling a large collection of cards here: <a href=\"https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/1715022/arcadia-wyld-hunt-950-cards-saletrade\" target=\"_blank\">https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/171...ards-saletrade</a> Maybe he can help?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12908-darkyeoman","name":"darkyeoman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:04:52-08:00","id":1046407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Keichiokami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1042684#post1042684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome! I love the website ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12908-darkyeoman","name":"darkyeoman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T23:06:50-08:00","id":1046649,"title":"","content":"Djinn card huh? So were they considering Genies as Changeling Kiths? People were fanmaking those back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T00:09:47-08:00","id":1046665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1046649#post1046649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Djinn card huh? So were they considering Genies as Changeling Kiths? People were fanmaking those back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of the kiths in Arcadia were unique to that game. But maybe we'll see them, and dragonkin, in C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T01:10:27-08:00","id":1046677,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't count on it, but the build-a-kith rules should make it easy to bring the unique kiths in the CCG over to the RPG.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, in the process of typing this post, I think I figured how I would do a dragonkin kith using C20's guidelines \ud83d\ude09 )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T02:05:09-08:00","id":1046688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1046677#post1046677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't count on it, but the build-a-kith rules should make it easy to bring the unique kiths in the CCG over to the RPG.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, in the process of typing this post, I think I figured how I would do a dragonkin kith using C20's guidelines \ud83d\ude09 )</div> </div> </div> </div>Once C20 is out, could you post your house rules for them using the build-your-own-kith rules? I had an outside hope that the difference between the announced number of kiths (110 was it?) and the amount we could all figure out from extant material (80?) might be made up of examples from the card game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T03:53:50-08:00","id":1046703,"title":"","content":"I'll talk to Matt about it. If there might be an opportunity to include new kiths in other books down the road, I'd rather save things for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:30:02-08:00","id":1046856,"title":"","content":"What were the new kiths asside from Djinn and Dragonkin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:43:49-08:00","id":1046863,"title":"","content":"The game had character cards. Some of them where obviously based on kiths, others were more like chimera, while others weren't creatures of Dream at all. Some of the ones that might translate to kiths that weren't kiths already are probably the dragonkin, djinn, imps, nymphs, and tritons.<br /> <br /> Things like the mechorg, renegade cogs, and army ant platoons would probably be chimera. There were also humans and fianna garou <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T15:09:55-08:00","id":1046940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1046856#post1046856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What were the new kiths asside from Djinn and Dragonkin?</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what PookaKnight said, there are also the following Naga, Ogre, Gremlin, and Mer (which were only later included in WoD, in <i>Blood Dimmed Tides</i>).<br /> <br /> I've often wondered how much of Arcadia would have made it into Changeling if the game had lasted longer. There are quite a few ideas from Arcadia that surfaced in <i>Blood Dimmed Tides, </i>for example: skycraft, mer(folk), tritons, rokea, etc. all first appeared in Arcadia, even though there isn't all that much ocean to explore in the two sets of cards that were produced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12908-darkyeoman","user":"darkyeoman","date":". 02-10-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12908-darkyeoman","name":"darkyeoman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T15:17:30-08:00","id":1046946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1046863#post1046863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were also humans and fianna garou <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding Garou in Arcadia, see this post by my &quot;co-curator&quot; of the blog, who is also a big WoD Werewolf fan: <a href=\"https://arcadiaccg.wordpress.com/2017/02/05/sands-of-sleep-card-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">https://arcadiaccg.wordpress.com/201...ep-card-notes/</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12908-darkyeoman","name":"darkyeoman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T15:39:56-08:00","id":1046955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1046863#post1046863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things like the mechorg, renegade cogs, and army ant platoons would probably be chimera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like awesome player characters to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T17:25:17-08:00","id":1046983,"title":"","content":"My desire to be the soul of a swarm of army ants bound in a human body has been thwarted....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T19:30:42-08:00","id":1047024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1046688#post1046688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once C20 is out, could you post your house rules for them using the build-your-own-kith rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I talked to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a>, and he encouraged me to post the kith write-up. There are a few things I need to emphasize though. First off, this is purely done as a fan work. It's not an official write-up by any means. If the dragonkin do appear in a later C20 book, there's a good chance they'd look pretty different, even if they were written by me.They'd have to fit the needs of the book and vision of the developer. Second, this is a quick and dirty write up. I haven't done an editing pass. There may be grammar, style, or spelling errors. Also, some parts of it may not work as expected. I'd especially want to see the Child of Ouroboros birthright in play before considering it ready. If you're still interested after C20 is out, remind me, and I'll be happy to walk through how I used the build-a-kith rules as a guide for the dragonkin.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Dragonkin</b><br /> <br /> Before the rise of humanity, the Tuatha de Danaan, or the Fomorians \u2014 before even the Mythic Ages \u2014 another civilization covered the world. They crafted legends in their own image. Now, sixty-five million years later, nothing remains of their existence, except their dreams. Without these Dreamers, the dragonkin were dwindling by the time the first human set foot upon Earth.<br /> <br /> The surviving dragonkin saw the Tuatha de Danaan amassing an army for war. They realized the Tuatha\u2019s plan to leverage humanity to overthrow the Fomorians held the key to their survival. The dragonkin offered themselves to the service of the Tuatha de Danaan in exchange for a place in humanity\u2019s collective psyche. As one of the Kithain, legends of dragons once again spread across the globe \u2014 from those of Europe to the Chinese dragons of southeast Asia to the feathered serpents of the Americas.<br /> <br /> Few in number to begin with, most dragonkin fled to Arcadia at the start of the Sundering. Only handfuls remained trapped on Earth during the Shattering. Their numbers in the Autumn Realms increased recently with the Resurgence. Dragonkin are reptilian humanoids, their skin glistening with scales. Their body types range from large and stocky to slim and lithe. Some even sport manes of brightly colored feathers.<br /> <br /> <b>Affinity:</b> Fae<br /> <br /> <b>Revelry:</b> A dragonkin finds Glamour in her prized possessions. They serve as a reminder and conduit to all that she once lost. By spending a day in meditation or a night sleeping surrounded by her treasures, she regains Glamour.<br /> <br /> <b>Unleashing:</b> Fire burns within a dragonkin\u2019s Glamour. Her Unleashings explode out from her, providing warm comfort to her allies and incinerating her enemies. They might take the form of steam, radiation, or a blazing inferno.<br /> <br /> <b>Birthrights:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom of Ages \u2014</b> A dragonkin has lived an impossibly long life, even by Kithain standards. She possesses knowledge unheard of by any other fae. All dragonkin have their Remembrance rating increased by one, even if it raises above five. Additionally, they cannot botch Enigmas or Gremayre rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Child of Ouroboros \u2014</b> In addition to her humanoid form, a dragonkin has a much older, true form inside her. Since the death of her original Dreamers and becoming tied to the dreams of humanity, it takes effort to bring forth. At character creation, the dragonkin\u2019s player receives 25 chimera points to spend on Attributes, Abilities, Health Levels, and Redes to become the character\u2019s dragon form. When the character assumes her dragon form, it adds to her normal stats. The character may spend a point of Glamour and roll Willpower (difficulty 6) to assume her dragon form for a scene. She may take her dragon form automatically when successfully Calling upon the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Treasure Hoard \u2014</b> The dragonkin lost everything once, never again. With nothing left of her original legend, a dragonkin\u2019s current treasures mean as much to her as her own life. If anyone attempts to steal or tamper with her possessions, she becomes consumed by rage. She immediately lashes out to attack those that would violate proof of her new dream. To restrain herself, she must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 7). If the item is a Treasure, the difficulty increases by one for each dot of the Treasure\u2019s rating, up to a maximum of 9.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWe were once powerless to avert the end of the world. Our fire will prevent the Endless Winter from consuming the new one.\u201d</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T19:51:33-08:00","id":1047029,"title":"","content":"That's one awesome write-up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T20:08:19-08:00","id":1047036,"title":"","content":"Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" s