d=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a> ! Insight into the Kith building rules AND a fan-writeup of the dragonkin using them?! This is a blessed day for the Dreaming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T20:02:35-08:00","id":1047507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1047024#post1047024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I talked to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a>, and he encouraged me to post the kith write-up. There are a few things I need to emphasize though. First off, this is purely done as a fan work. It's not an official write-up by any means. If the dragonkin do appear in a later C20 book, there's a good chance they'd look pretty different, even if they were written by me.They'd have to fit the needs of the book and vision of the developer. Second, this is a quick and dirty write up. I haven't done an editing pass. There may be grammar, style, or spelling errors. Also, some parts of it may not work as expected. I'd especially want to see the Child of Ouroboros birthright in play before considering it ready. If you're still interested after C20 is out, remind me, and I'll be happy to walk through how I used the build-a-kith rules as a guide for the dragonkin.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Dragonkin</b><br /> <br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow! That is a great write-up. How did I not know that kith existed? I think the draconic form is a neat touch, although I'd worry that 25 points might prove a bit potent. Then again, for an ancient dragon, a lot of power could also be quite appropriate, so perhaps I'm overthinking that. Thank you so much for sharing this. I'll need to post my write-up for a similar kith (and its Thallain equivalent) at some point in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T03:30:52-08:00","id":1047632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1047507#post1047507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the draconic form is a neat touch, although I'd worry that 25 points might prove a bit potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, and absolutely. That's why I'd want to see it in action - it would help me fine tune the number of points to build the dragon form. It's about the equivalent of a two dot chimera, but since it gets added to the PC's traits instead of being a separate entity, it's entirely possible to funnel all those points into a single trait.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, you should definitely post your kiths!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T07:42:42-08:00","id":1047698,"title":"","content":"I'd give my right arm to know what happened to High King Ardlanth's Court and what is the Darkening. The Lion's Den should be a future kickstart project. &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T08:07:54-08:00","id":1047706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1047632#post1047632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, and absolutely. That's why I'd want to see it in action - it would help me fine tune the number of points to build the dragon form. It's about the equivalent of a two dot chimera, but since it gets added to the PC's traits instead of being a separate entity, it's entirely possible to funnel all those points into a single trait.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, you should definitely post your kiths!</div> </div> </div> </div>That was exactly what I'd been thinking. It would be quite easy to dump a bunch of points into, say, Strength, putting any Troll or even a Gurahl to shame, and still have some left for stamina, armor, and fire breath.<br /> <br /> I will definitely post my kiths. I've been refining their write-up for awhile now. I just need to wait a bit longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T19:44:15-08:00","id":1048038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1047706#post1047706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was exactly what I'd been thinking. It would be quite easy to dump a bunch of points into, say, Strength, putting any Troll or even a Gurahl to shame, and still have some left for stamina, armor, and fire breath.<br /> <br /> I will definitely post my kiths. I've been refining their write-up for awhile now. I just need to wait a bit longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>a Troll's strength is always there. the Dragonkin has a pretty nice &quot;NOW YOU FACE MY TRUE FORM&quot; Power but its pretty costly to use with impunity(though Trolls could use a buff so its not &quot;Be old FTW&quot;)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T20:05:18-08:00","id":1048047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1048038#post1048038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Dragonkin has a pretty nice &amp;quot;NOW YOU FACE MY TRUE FORM&amp;quot; Power but its pretty costly to use with impunity</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my intention, but I think White Oak Dragon is right. I forgot how cheap Attributes and Health Levels are in chimera points. The intention was to be able to afford a couple of redes and a handful of Attributes, Abilities, and/or Health Levels. Something like 10 chimera points would probably be more appropriate for that than the 25.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T21:24:34-08:00","id":1048061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia-the-wyld-hunt-king-ironheart-s-madness?p=1048047#post1048047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my intention, but I think White Oak Dragon is right. I forgot how cheap Attributes and Health Levels are in chimera points. The intention was to be able to afford a couple of redes and a handful of Attributes, Abilities, and/or Health Levels. Something like 10 chimera points would probably be more appropriate for that than the 25.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would it be balanced to build your dragonform as you grow in xp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:03:07-08:00","id":1048130,"title":"","content":"The dragon form kind of does grow as the character accumulates xp because the extra Traits from the dragon form add to the character's normal Traits. A strength 2 character with +3 strength dots in his dragon form has 5 strength when he goes dragon. If he raises his strength to 3, he'll have 6 strength when he goes dragon.<br /> <br /> Going from 25 to 10 sounds like a huge reduction, but for whatever reason, I thought Attributes cost at least 1 chimera point per dot. They're actually 3 dots per chimera point. Even reduced to 10 points, that's still potentially 30 extra Attribute dots. If the player takes a couple of Redes, he'll still likely have 2 or 3 points left which would be either 6 or 9 additional Attribute dots. That's a pretty huge bonus no matter how you slice it - certainly worthy of any NOW YOU SEE MY TRUE POWER moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T18:17:35-08:00","id":1048513,"title":"","content":"The problem is that while Attributes are underpriced, most of the Redes are overpriced. Building a chimera quickly turns into a mini-game of getting rid of all the Redes, that might be interesting narratively and concept-wise, but not that much needed, when you look at the cost and want to build somewhat balanced character (while building a ridiculously overpowered one trick pony chimera is not easy, it's super easy - meat Rex-Zilla The Giant Tele-operated Toy - Will/Social/Mental 0. Strength 10. Stamina 10. Dexterity 4. Fight 6. Athletics 3. Health 8. Glamour 10. - 25 points, that's from the top of my head). So, I hope you did take a look at chimera creation costs.<br /> <br /> Adding Chimera points to the existing character can make the process a bit more balanced, though there are still some questions left. Chimera traits are limited by their Glamour rating, Glamour costs 1=1, so that will eat some of the points, which also leaves a question, does it mean that character gets extra temp Glamour she can use? Because I must tell you, Redes burn Glamour really fast.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar648_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"648\" data-vbnamecard=\"648\">PookaKnight</a>, could you maybe start a new topic and repost your kith there? If not before c20's release, than after it we can discuss it there in details 'on-topic'. ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 02-13-2017, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T06:09:51-08:00","id":1048708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1039900-arcadia